\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The block-matrix chart of the Schur factorization}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Choose ordered bases of the retained and eliminated summands
in \ref{fdip-009J}, eliminated generators second. The typed
compressions become the blocks of one matrix
#{K=\left(\begin{smallmatrix}A&B\\C&D\end{smallmatrix}\right)}.
The finite block identity is then the chart
\leanref{Matrix.det_fromBlocks₂₂}, for finite index types over
a commutative ring with an invertible eliminated block. This
formal statement supports the determinant factorization. It
does not supply the partial Grassmann coefficient.}
